/-!
# The total site of a simplicial object of a site over an object

Let `C` be a site with fibre products, let `X` be an object of `C`, let `U` be a simplicial
object of `C` and let `a : U ⟶ X` be an augmentation. From `U` one obtains the simplicial
semi-representable object `K` of `SR(C, X)` with `K_n = {U_n ⟶ X}`, and the constructions
attached to a simplicial semi-representable object over `X` give a total site `(C/K)_total` and
an augmentation morphism of topoi `Sh((C/K)_total) ⟶ Sh(C/X)`, the morphism of topoi of the
localization functor `j_total`.

More precisely, the site `(C/U)_total` has as objects the objects `V/U_n` of the localizations
`C/U_n`, and a morphism `(φ, f) : V/U_n ⟶ W/U_m` is a simplex map `φ : [m] ⟶ [n]` together with
a morphism `f : V ⟶ W` of `C` such that `f ≫ (W ⟶ U_m) = (V ⟶ U_n) ≫ f_φ`; its coverings are the
families lying in one simplicial degree which are coverings of `C/U_n`. The augmentation is the
morphism of topoi of the cocontinuous functor `V/U_n ↦ V/X`. This file proves that the two
descriptions agree: the iterated slice equivalences `(C/X)/{U_n ⟶ X} ≌ C/U_n` assemble into an
equivalence of sites `(C/K)_total ≌ (C/U)_total`, under which the localization functor `j_total`
is the functor `V/U_n ↦ V/X`, and hence under which the two augmentation morphisms of topoi
`Sh((C/U)_total) ⟶ Sh(C/X)` agree.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.homEquivCommSq`: a morphism `V/U_n ⟶ W/U_m` of `(C/U)_total`
  is a pair `(φ, f)` making the square with `f_φ` commute.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.fromAssociatedTotal` and `.toAssociatedTotal`: the comparison
  functors between `(C/K)_total` and `(C/U)_total`, induced by the degreewise iterated slice
  functors `fromComponentOver` and `toComponentOver`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.associatedTotalEquivalence`: the equivalence of categories
  `(C/K)_total ≌ (C/U)_total`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.associatedTotalSheafEquivalence`: the induced equivalence of
  topoi `Sh((C/K)_total) ≌ Sh((C/U)_total)`.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.associatedTotalEquivalence_isDenseSubsite` and
  `.functorPushforward_fromAssociatedTotal_mem_iff`: the equivalence identifies the coverings of
  the two total sites.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.toAssociatedTotal_comp_totalForget`: under the identification,
  the localization functor `j_total : (C/K)_total ⥤ C/X` is the functor `V/U_n ↦ V/X`.
* `CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver.augmentationPushforwardIsoAssociated` and
  `.augmentationInverseImageIsoAssociated`: the augmentation morphism of topoi given by
  `V/U_n ↦ V/X` is the augmentation morphism of topoi of `(C/K)_total`, transported along the
  equivalence of topoi.

## Implementation notes

The source identifies the two total sites; here they are distinct categories, the Grothendieck
constructions of `n ↦ C/U_n` and of `n ↦ ∐_{i} (C/X)/K_{n,i}`, and the identification is an
equivalence of categories which is cocontinuous in both directions. Its two halves are induced by
strict morphisms of simplicial diagrams of categories: `C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n` is strictly natural on
the nose, while naturality of `C/U_n ⥤ C/K_n` holds because `f_φ ≫ a_m = a_n`, and is an
equality of functors proved after composition with the faithful functor `C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n`. The
composite `C/U_n ⥤ C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n` is the identity, so `(C/U)_total ⥤ (C/K)_total` is a section of
the fully faithful functor `(C/K)_total ⥤ (C/U)_total`.

The results are stated for an arbitrary topology `J` on `C`; the topology used for the
hypercovering conditions, generated by a pretopology `P`, is the case `J = P.toGrothendieck`, in
which `CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalSituation P U a` and
`CategoryTheory.SimplicialSemiRepresentable.augmentationMorphismOfTopoi P U a` are the total site
and the morphism of topoi of `(C/K)_total` used here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Section 09X8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09X8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0D8C](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0D8C)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GM9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GM9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite Simplicial SemiRepresentable
  Stacks.CategoryTheory.Hypercovering

universe u

namespace CategoryTheory.Grothendieck

variable {E : Type*} [Category E] {F G : E ⥤ Cat.{u, u}}

/-- The functor induced on Grothendieck constructions by a natural transformation with
faithful components is faithful. -/
theorem faithful_map (α : F ⟶ G) (h : ∀ c, (α.app c).toFunctor.Faithful) :
    (Grothendieck.map α).Faithful where
  map_injective {x y} f g hfg := by
    obtain ⟨fb, ff⟩ := f
    obtain ⟨gb, gf⟩ := g
    have hb : fb = gb := congrArg Hom.base hfg
    subst hb
    injection hfg with _ hfib
    simp only [Cat.eqToHom_app, cancel_epi] at hfib
    congr
    exact (α.app y.base).toFunctor.map_injective hfib

/-- The functor induced on Grothendieck constructions by a natural transformation with full
components is full. -/
theorem full_map (α : F ⟶ G) (h : ∀ c, (α.app c).toFunctor.Full) :
    (Grothendieck.map α).Full where
  map_surjective {x y} g := by
    have e : (α.app y.base).toFunctor.obj ((F.map g.base).toFunctor.obj x.fiber) =
        (G.map g.base).toFunctor.obj ((α.app x.base).toFunctor.obj x.fiber) :=
      Functor.congr_obj (congrArg Cat.Hom.toFunctor (α.naturality g.base)) x.fiber
    refine ⟨⟨g.base, (α.app y.base).toFunctor.preimage (eqToHom e ≫ g.fiber)⟩, ?_⟩
    refine Grothendieck.ext _ _ rfl ?_
    dsimp only [map] at g e ⊢
    simp only [Cat.eqToHom_app, Functor.map_preimage, eqToHom_trans_assoc]
    exact (eqToHom_trans_assoc _ _ _).trans (Category.id_comp g.fiber)

/-- Precomposing a functor out of a Grothendieck construction, built from fibrewise functors
whose transitions are transports along equalities, with the functor induced by a natural
transformation `α` gives the functor built from the fibrewise composites with `α`. -/
theorem map_comp_functorFromOfEq {D : Type*} [Category D] (α : F ⟶ G) (fib : ∀ c, G.obj c ⥤ D)
    (e : ∀ {c c' : E} (f : c ⟶ c'), fib c = (G.map f).toFunctor ⋙ fib c') (hom_id hom_comp)
    (e' : ∀ {c c' : E} (f : c ⟶ c'),
      (α.app c).toFunctor ⋙ fib c = (F.map f).toFunctor ⋙ (α.app c').toFunctor ⋙ fib c')
    (hom_id' hom_comp') :
    Grothendieck.map α ⋙ functorFromOfEq fib (fun f ↦ eqToHom (e f)) hom_id hom_comp =
      functorFromOfEq (fun c ↦ (α.app c).toFunctor ⋙ fib c) (fun f ↦ eqToHom (e' f))
        hom_id' hom_comp' := by
  refine Functor.hext (fun _ ↦ rfl) fun x y f ↦ heq_of_eq ?_
  dsimp only [Functor.comp_map, functorFromOfEq, map]
  simp only [eqToHom_app, Cat.eqToHom_app, Functor.map_comp, eqToHom_map, eqToHom_trans_assoc]

end CategoryTheory.Grothendieck

namespace CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver

variable {C : Type u} [SmallCategory C] [HasPullbacks C] {X : C} (U : SimplicialObject C)
  (a : U ⟶ (SimplicialObject.const C).obj X)

/-- A morphism `V/U_n ⟶ W/U_m` of `(C/U)_total` is a pair `(φ, f)` of a simplex map
`φ : [m] ⟶ [n]` and a morphism `f : V ⟶ W` of `C` such that the square formed with `V ⟶ U_n`,
`W ⟶ U_m` and `f_φ : U_n ⟶ U_m` commutes. -/
@[stacks 09X8 "a morphism (φ, f) : V/U_n → W/U_m of (C/U)_total is φ : [m] → [n] and f : V → W \
with commutative square"]
def homEquivCommSq (A B : Grothendieck (slices U)) :
    (A ⟶ B) ≃ {p : (A.base ⟶ B.base) × ((A.fiber : Over (U.obj A.base)).left ⟶
        (B.fiber : Over (U.obj B.base)).left) //
      p.2 ≫ (B.fiber : Over (U.obj B.base)).hom = (A.fiber : Over (U.obj A.base)).hom ≫ U.map p.1}
    where
  toFun f := ⟨(f.base, f.fiber.left), Over.w f.fiber⟩
  invFun p := ⟨p.1.1, Over.homMk p.1.2 p.2⟩
  left_inv _ := rfl
  right_inv _ := rfl

/-- The degree `n` comparison functor `C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n`: the component `C/K_n` is the single
slice `(C/X)/{U_n ⟶ X}`, and the functor is the iterated slice functor to `C/U_n`. -/
def fromComponentOver (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    ComponentOver ((associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a).obj n) ⥤ Over (U.obj n) :=
  CategoryTheory.Sigma.desc fun _ ↦ Over.iteratedSliceForward ((Over.lift U a).obj n)

/-- The degree `n` comparison functor `C/U_n ⥤ C/K_n`, the iterated slice functor
`V/U_n ↦ (V/X)/(U_n/X)`. -/
def toComponentOver (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    Over (U.obj n) ⥤ ComponentOver ((associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a).obj n) :=
  Over.iteratedSliceBackward ((Over.lift U a).obj n) ⋙
    CategoryTheory.Sigma.incl (C := fun _ : PUnit.{u + 1} ↦ Over ((Over.lift U a).obj n))
      PUnit.unit

/-- The degree `n` comparison functor `C/U_n ⥤ C/K_n` is a section of `C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n`. -/
theorem toComponentOver_comp_fromComponentOver (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    toComponentOver U a n ⋙ fromComponentOver U a n = 𝟭 _ :=
  rfl

/-- The degreewise comparison functors `C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n` commute with the transition functors. -/
theorem componentOverMap_comp_fromComponentOver {m n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ} (α : m ⟶ n) :
    componentOverMap ((associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a).map α) ⋙ fromComponentOver U a n =
      fromComponentOver U a m ⋙ Over.map (U.map α) := by
  refine Functor.hext (fun _ ↦ rfl) ?_
  rintro ⟨⟨⟩, x⟩ ⟨⟨⟩, y⟩ ⟨f⟩
  rfl

/-- The degreewise comparison functors `C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n`, as a morphism of simplicial diagrams of
categories. -/
def fromSlices :
    SimplicialSemiRepresentable.slices (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a) ⟶ slices U where
  app n := (fromComponentOver U a n).toCatHom
  naturality _m _n α := Cat.Hom.ext (componentOverMap_comp_fromComponentOver U a α)

/-- The degree `n` comparison functor `C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n` is faithful. -/
instance faithful_fromComponentOver (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    (fromComponentOver U a n).Faithful where
  map_injective {x y} f g h := by
    obtain ⟨⟨⟩, x⟩ := x
    obtain ⟨⟨⟩, y⟩ := y
    obtain ⟨f⟩ := f
    obtain ⟨g⟩ := g
    exact congrArg CategoryTheory.Sigma.SigmaHom.mk
      ((Over.iteratedSliceEquiv ((Over.lift U a).obj n)).functor.map_injective h)

/-- The degree `n` comparison functor `C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n` is full. -/
instance full_fromComponentOver (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) : (fromComponentOver U a n).Full where
  map_surjective {x y} g := by
    obtain ⟨⟨⟩, x⟩ := x
    obtain ⟨⟨⟩, y⟩ := y
    exact ⟨CategoryTheory.Sigma.SigmaHom.mk
      ((Over.iteratedSliceEquiv ((Over.lift U a).obj n)).functor.preimage g),
      (Over.iteratedSliceEquiv ((Over.lift U a).obj n)).functor.map_preimage g⟩

/-- Two functors which agree on objects and become equal after composition with a faithful
functor are equal. -/
theorem _root_.CategoryTheory.Functor.ext_of_comp_eq_of_faithful {A B D : Type*} [Category A]
    [Category B] [Category D] {G₁ G₂ : A ⥤ B} (ψ : B ⥤ D) [ψ.Faithful]
    (hobj : ∀ x, G₁.obj x = G₂.obj x) (h : G₁ ⋙ ψ = G₂ ⋙ ψ) : G₁ = G₂ := by
  refine Functor.ext hobj fun x y f ↦ ψ.map_injective ?_
  have hf := Functor.congr_hom h f
  simp only [Functor.comp_map] at hf
  rw [hf, Functor.map_comp, Functor.map_comp, eqToHom_map, eqToHom_map]

omit [HasPullbacks C] in
/-- Two objects of an iterated slice given by morphisms with equal sources and equal underlying
morphisms are equal. -/
theorem _root_.CategoryTheory.Over.mk_eq_mk {Z A B : Over X} (h : A = B) (f : A ⟶ Z) (g : B ⟶ Z)
    (hfg : f.left = eqToHom (congrArg Comma.left h) ≫ g.left) :
    Over.mk f = Over.mk g := by
  subst h
  simp only [eqToHom_refl, Category.id_comp] at hfg
  rw [Over.OverMorphism.ext hfg]

omit [HasPullbacks C] in
/-- The object equality underlying the naturality of `toComponentOver`. -/
theorem toComponentOver_naturality_source {m n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ} (α : m ⟶ n)
    (V : Over (U.obj m)) :
    Over.mk ((V.hom ≫ U.map α) ≫ a.app n) = Over.mk (V.hom ≫ a.app m) := by
  rw [Category.assoc]
  exact congrArg (fun g ↦ Over.mk (V.hom ≫ g)) (augmentationApp_naturality U a α)

/-- The degreewise comparison functors `C/U_n ⥤ C/K_n` commute with the transition functors;
this uses `f_φ ≫ a_m = a_n`. -/
theorem toComponentOver_naturality {m n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ} (α : m ⟶ n) :
    Over.map (U.map α) ⋙ toComponentOver U a n =
      toComponentOver U a m ⋙ componentOverMap ((associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a).map α) := by
  refine Functor.ext_of_comp_eq_of_faithful (fromComponentOver U a n)
    (fun V ↦ congrArg (Sigma.mk PUnit.unit)
      (Over.mk_eq_mk (toComponentOver_naturality_source U a α V) _ _
        (Category.id_comp _).symm)) ?_
  rw [Functor.assoc (toComponentOver U a m), componentOverMap_comp_fromComponentOver]
  rfl

/-- The degreewise comparison functors `C/U_n ⥤ C/K_n`, as a morphism of simplicial diagrams of
categories. -/
def toSlices :
    slices U ⟶ SimplicialSemiRepresentable.slices (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a) where
  app n := (toComponentOver U a n).toCatHom
  naturality _m _n α := Cat.Hom.ext (toComponentOver_naturality U a α)

/-- The morphism `toSlices` is a section of `fromSlices`. -/
theorem toSlices_comp_fromSlices : toSlices U a ≫ fromSlices U a = 𝟙 _ :=
  rfl

/-- The comparison functor `(C/K)_total ⥤ (C/U)_total`. -/
def fromAssociatedTotal : Grothendieck (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.slices
    (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a)) ⥤ Grothendieck (slices U) :=
  Grothendieck.map (fromSlices U a)

/-- The comparison functor `(C/U)_total ⥤ (C/K)_total`. -/
def toAssociatedTotal : Grothendieck (slices U) ⥤ Grothendieck (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.slices
    (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a)) :=
  Grothendieck.map (toSlices U a)

/-- The comparison functor `(C/U)_total ⥤ (C/K)_total` is a section of the comparison functor
`(C/K)_total ⥤ (C/U)_total`. -/
theorem toAssociatedTotal_comp_fromAssociatedTotal :
    toAssociatedTotal U a ⋙ fromAssociatedTotal U a = 𝟭 _ := by
  rw [toAssociatedTotal, fromAssociatedTotal, ← Grothendieck.map_comp_eq,
    toSlices_comp_fromSlices, Grothendieck.map_id_eq]

/-- The comparison functor `(C/K)_total ⥤ (C/U)_total` is faithful. -/
instance faithful_fromAssociatedTotal : (fromAssociatedTotal U a).Faithful :=
  Grothendieck.faithful_map _ fun n ↦ inferInstanceAs (fromComponentOver U a n).Faithful

/-- The comparison functor `(C/K)_total ⥤ (C/U)_total` is full. -/
instance full_fromAssociatedTotal : (fromAssociatedTotal U a).Full :=
  Grothendieck.full_map _ fun n ↦ inferInstanceAs (fromComponentOver U a n).Full

/-- The comparison functor `(C/K)_total ⥤ (C/U)_total` is essentially surjective. -/
instance essSurj_fromAssociatedTotal : (fromAssociatedTotal U a).EssSurj where
  mem_essImage Y := ⟨(toAssociatedTotal U a).obj Y,
    ⟨eqToIso (Functor.congr_obj (toAssociatedTotal_comp_fromAssociatedTotal U a) Y)⟩⟩

/-- The comparison functor `(C/K)_total ⥤ (C/U)_total` is an equivalence of categories. -/
instance isEquivalence_fromAssociatedTotal : (fromAssociatedTotal U a).IsEquivalence where

/-- Under the identification of `(C/U)_total` with `(C/K)_total`, the localization functor
`j_total : (C/K)_total ⥤ C/X` is the functor `V/U_n ↦ V/X`: precomposed with
`(C/U)_total ⥤ (C/K)_total` it is `augmentationFunctor` on the nose. -/
@[stacks 09X8 "the morphism of topoi a is given by the cocontinuous functor V/U_n ↦ V/X: \
j_total of (C/K)_total is V/U_n ↦ V/X under the identification"]
theorem toAssociatedTotal_comp_totalForget :
    toAssociatedTotal U a ⋙
        SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalForget (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a) =
      augmentationFunctor U a := by
  have hfib : ∀ c, ((toSlices U a).app c).toFunctor ⋙
      SimplicialSemiRepresentable.sliceForget (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a) c =
        augmentationFibre U a c := fun _ ↦ Functor.ext (fun _ ↦ rfl) (fun _ _ g ↦ by
          apply Over.OverMorphism.ext
          simp only [Over.comp_left]
          exact (Category.comp_id _).symm.trans (Category.id_comp _).symm)
  rw [toAssociatedTotal, SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalForget,
    Grothendieck.map_comp_functorFromOfEq (toSlices U a) _ _ _ _
      (fun f ↦ by rw [hfib, hfib]; exact augmentationFibre_eq U a f)
    (fun _ ↦ rfl) (fun _ _ _ _ _ ↦ by rw [Functor.whiskerLeft_eqToHom, eqToHom_trans,
      eqToHom_trans])]
  exact Grothendieck.functorFromOfEq_congr _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ (funext hfib)

section Site

variable (J : GrothendieckTopology C)

/-- The topology of the total site `(C/K)_total` attached to the simplicial
semi-representable object `K` with `K_n = {U_n ⟶ X}`, on the Grothendieck construction. -/
abbrev associatedTotalTopology :
    GrothendieckTopology
      (Grothendieck (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.slices (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a))) :=
  (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.situation (J.over X)
    (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a)).totalTopology

omit [HasPullbacks C] in
/-- The degree `n` comparison functor `C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n` is cocontinuous. -/
theorem fromComponentOver_isCocontinuous (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    (fromComponentOver U a n).IsCocontinuous
      (componentwiseTopology (J.over X) ((associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a).obj n))
      (J.over (U.obj n)) where
  cover_lift {x} S hS := by
    obtain ⟨⟨⟩, x⟩ := x
    exact (Over.iteratedSliceForward ((Over.lift U a).obj n)).cover_lift
      ((J.over X).over _) (J.over _) hS

omit [HasPullbacks C] in
/-- The degree `n` comparison functor `C/U_n ⥤ C/K_n` is cocontinuous. -/
theorem toComponentOver_isCocontinuous (n : SimplexCategoryᵒᵖ) :
    (toComponentOver U a n).IsCocontinuous (J.over (U.obj n))
      (componentwiseTopology (J.over X) ((associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a).obj n)) where
  cover_lift hS := (Over.iteratedSliceBackward ((Over.lift U a).obj n)).cover_lift
    (J.over ((Over.lift U a).obj n).left) ((J.over X).over ((Over.lift U a).obj n))
    ((Stacks.Cohomology.SimplicialSummand.incl_isCocontinuous (J.over X)
      ((associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a).obj n) PUnit.unit).cover_lift hS)

/-- The degreewise comparison functors `C/K_n ⥤ C/U_n`, as a morphism of simplicial sites. -/
def fromSimplicialSite :
    CocontinuousSimplicialSite.Morphism
      (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.simplicialSite (J.over X) (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a))
      (simplicialSite J U) where
  hom := fromSlices U a
  isCocontinuous n := by
    change (fromComponentOver U a n).IsCocontinuous
      (topologyOfCoverings (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.sliceCoverings (J.over X)
        (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a) n)) (topologyOfCoverings (sliceCoverings J U n))
    rw [SimplicialSemiRepresentable.topologyOfCoverings_sliceCoverings,
      topologyOfCoverings_sliceCoverings]
    exact fromComponentOver_isCocontinuous U a J n

/-- The degreewise comparison functors `C/U_n ⥤ C/K_n`, as a morphism of simplicial sites. -/
def toSimplicialSite :
    CocontinuousSimplicialSite.Morphism (simplicialSite J U)
      (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.simplicialSite (J.over X)
        (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a)) where
  hom := toSlices U a
  isCocontinuous n := by
    change (toComponentOver U a n).IsCocontinuous (topologyOfCoverings (sliceCoverings J U n))
      (topologyOfCoverings (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.sliceCoverings (J.over X)
        (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a) n))
    rw [SimplicialSemiRepresentable.topologyOfCoverings_sliceCoverings,
      topologyOfCoverings_sliceCoverings]
    exact toComponentOver_isCocontinuous U a J n

/-- The comparison functor `(C/K)_total ⥤ (C/U)_total` is cocontinuous. -/
instance fromAssociatedTotal_isCocontinuous :
    (fromAssociatedTotal U a).IsCocontinuous
      (associatedTotalTopology U a J) (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) :=
  (fromSimplicialSite U a J).totalFunctor_isCocontinuous

/-- The comparison functor `(C/U)_total ⥤ (C/K)_total` is cocontinuous. -/
instance toAssociatedTotal_isCocontinuous :
    (toAssociatedTotal U a).IsCocontinuous (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U)
      (associatedTotalTopology U a J) :=
  (toSimplicialSite U a J).totalFunctor_isCocontinuous

/-- The equivalence of categories `(C/K)_total ≌ (C/U)_total` between the total site attached
to `K` and the category whose objects are the `V/U_n` and whose morphisms are the pairs `(φ, f)`.
Its functor is `fromAssociatedTotal`, and its inverse is `toAssociatedTotal` by
`associatedTotalEquivalenceInverseIso`. -/
@[stacks 09X8 "the site (C/U)_total, with objects V/U_n and morphisms (φ, f), is (C/K)_total of \
Remark 0D8C: the equivalence of categories"]
def associatedTotalEquivalence :
    Grothendieck (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.slices (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a)) ≌
      Grothendieck (slices U) :=
  (fromAssociatedTotal U a).asEquivalence

/-- The inverse of `associatedTotalEquivalence` is `toAssociatedTotal`. -/
def associatedTotalEquivalenceInverseIso :
    (associatedTotalEquivalence U a).inverse ≅ toAssociatedTotal U a :=
  (Functor.leftUnitor _).symm ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerRight (eqToIso (toAssociatedTotal_comp_fromAssociatedTotal U a).symm) _ ≪≫
    Functor.associator _ _ _ ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerLeft (toAssociatedTotal U a)
      (associatedTotalEquivalence U a).unitIso.symm ≪≫
    Functor.rightUnitor _

/-- The equivalence `(C/K)_total ≌ (C/U)_total` identifies the topologies: it is a dense subsite
inclusion, so a sieve is covering exactly when its image is. -/
@[stacks 09X8 "the site (C/U)_total is (C/K)_total of Remark 0D8C: the coverings agree"]
theorem associatedTotalEquivalence_isDenseSubsite :
    (associatedTotalEquivalence U a).functor.IsDenseSubsite
      (associatedTotalTopology U a J) (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) :=
  have h₁ : (associatedTotalEquivalence U a).functor.IsCocontinuous
      (associatedTotalTopology U a J) (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) :=
    fromAssociatedTotal_isCocontinuous U a J
  have h₂ : (associatedTotalEquivalence U a).inverse.IsCocontinuous
      (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) (associatedTotalTopology U a J) :=
    have := toAssociatedTotal_isCocontinuous U a J
    Functor.IsCocontinuous.of_iso (associatedTotalEquivalenceInverseIso U a).symm
  @Equivalence.isDenseSubsite_functor_of_isCocontinuous _ _ _ _ _ _
    (associatedTotalEquivalence U a) h₁ h₂

/-- A sieve of `(C/K)_total` is covering exactly when its image in `(C/U)_total` is. -/
theorem functorPushforward_fromAssociatedTotal_mem_iff
    {x : Grothendieck (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.slices (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a))}
    (S : Sieve x) :
    S.functorPushforward (fromAssociatedTotal U a) ∈
        SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U ((fromAssociatedTotal U a).obj x) ↔
      S ∈ associatedTotalTopology U a J x :=
  (associatedTotalEquivalence_isDenseSubsite U a J).functorPushforward_mem_iff

/-- The direct image of the augmentation given by `V/U_n ↦ V/X` is the direct image along
`(C/U)_total ⥤ (C/K)_total` followed by the direct image of the augmentation of `(C/K)_total`. -/
def augmentationPushforwardIsoComp :
    (augmentationMorphismOfTopoi J U a).pushforward ≅
      (toAssociatedTotal U a).sheafPushforwardCocontinuous (Type u)
          (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) (associatedTotalTopology U a J) ⋙
        (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalLocalizationMorphism (J.over X)
          (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a)).pushforward :=
  haveI : (toAssociatedTotal U a ⋙ SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalForget
      (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a)).IsCocontinuous (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U)
        (J.over X) :=
    haveI := toAssociatedTotal_isCocontinuous U a J
    isCocontinuous_comp _ _ _ (associatedTotalTopology U a J)
  haveI := toAssociatedTotal_isCocontinuous U a J
  eqToIso (augmentationMorphismOfTopoi_pushforward J U a) ≪≫
    SimplicialSiteSituation.cocontinuousPushforwardIsoOfEq.{u, u, u, u, u}
      (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) (J.over X)
      (toAssociatedTotal_comp_totalForget U a).symm ≪≫
    sheafPushforwardCocontinuousCompIso (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U)
      (associatedTotalTopology U a J) (J.over X) (toAssociatedTotal U a)
      (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalForget (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a))

/-- `toAssociatedTotal` is left adjoint to `fromAssociatedTotal`. -/
def toAssociatedTotalAdjunction : toAssociatedTotal U a ⊣ fromAssociatedTotal U a :=
  (associatedTotalEquivalence U a).symm.toAdjunction.ofNatIsoLeft
    (associatedTotalEquivalenceInverseIso U a)

/-- The inverse of `associatedTotalEquivalence` is a dense subsite inclusion. -/
instance associatedTotalEquivalence_inverse_isDenseSubsite :
    (associatedTotalEquivalence U a).inverse.IsDenseSubsite (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U)
      (associatedTotalTopology U a J) :=
  haveI := toAssociatedTotal_isCocontinuous U a J
  haveI : (associatedTotalEquivalence U a).inverse.IsCocontinuous
      (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) (associatedTotalTopology U a J) :=
    Functor.IsCocontinuous.of_iso (associatedTotalEquivalenceInverseIso U a).symm
  haveI : (associatedTotalEquivalence U a).functor.IsCocontinuous (associatedTotalTopology U a J)
      (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) := fromAssociatedTotal_isCocontinuous U a J
  Equivalence.isDenseSubsite_inverse_of_isCocontinuous _ _ _

/-- The equivalence of topoi `Sh((C/K)_total) ≌ Sh((C/U)_total)` induced by the identification
of the two total sites. -/
def associatedTotalSheafEquivalence :
    Sheaf (associatedTotalTopology U a J) (Type u) ≌
      Sheaf (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) (Type u) :=
  (associatedTotalEquivalence U a).sheafCongr _ _ (Type u)

/-- The direct image along `(C/U)_total ⥤ (C/K)_total` is the inverse of
`associatedTotalSheafEquivalence`. -/
def toAssociatedTotalPushforwardIso :
    (toAssociatedTotal U a).sheafPushforwardCocontinuous (Type u)
        (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) (associatedTotalTopology U a J) ≅
      (associatedTotalSheafEquivalence U a J).inverse :=
  haveI := toAssociatedTotal_isCocontinuous U a J
  ((fullyFaithfulSheafToPresheaf (associatedTotalTopology U a J) (Type u)).whiskeringRight
    _).preimageIso (Functor.sheafPushforwardCocontinuousIsoRestriction (Type u)
      (SimplicialOver.totalTopology J U) (associatedTotalTopology U a J)
      (toAssociatedTotalAdjunction U a))

/-- The direct image of the augmentation `a : Sh((C/U)_total) ⟶ Sh(C/X)` given by
`V/U_n ↦ V/X` is the direct image of the morphism of topoi `Sh((C/K)_total) ⟶ Sh(C/X)` induced
by the total site of `K`, transported along `associatedTotalSheafEquivalence`. -/
@[stacks 09X8 "the augmentation morphism of topoi a : Sh((C/U)_total) → Sh(C/X): the one of \
Remark 0D8C and the one of V/U_n ↦ V/X agree, direct images"]
def augmentationPushforwardIsoAssociated :
    (augmentationMorphismOfTopoi J U a).pushforward ≅
      (associatedTotalSheafEquivalence U a J).inverse ⋙
        (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalLocalizationMorphism (J.over X)
          (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a)).pushforward :=
  augmentationPushforwardIsoComp U a J ≪≫
    Functor.isoWhiskerRight (toAssociatedTotalPushforwardIso U a J) _

/-- The inverse image of the augmentation `a : Sh((C/U)_total) ⟶ Sh(C/X)` is the inverse image
of the morphism of topoi `Sh((C/K)_total) ⟶ Sh(C/X)` followed by
`associatedTotalSheafEquivalence`. -/
@[stacks 09X8 "the augmentation morphism of topoi a : Sh((C/U)_total) → Sh(C/X): the one of \
Remark 0D8C and the one of V/U_n ↦ V/X agree, inverse images"]
def augmentationInverseImageIsoAssociated :
    (augmentationMorphismOfTopoi J U a).inverseImage ≅
      (SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalLocalizationMorphism (J.over X)
          (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a)).inverseImage ⋙
        (associatedTotalSheafEquivalence U a J).functor :=
  Adjunction.leftAdjointUniq (augmentationMorphismOfTopoi J U a).adj
    (((SimplicialSemiRepresentable.totalLocalizationMorphism (J.over X)
      (associatedSimplicialObject.{u} U a)).adj.comp
        (associatedTotalSheafEquivalence U a J).toAdjunction).ofNatIsoRight
      (augmentationPushforwardIsoAssociated U a J).symm)

end Site

end CategoryTheory.SimplicialOver

